.TH PHONE-CLI 1 "2026-07-12" "mcp-server-adb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phone-cli \- command-line interface to control an Android phone via ADB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phone-cli
.RI [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.RI [ \-d | \-\-debug ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phone-cli
is a direct command-line interface to the same phone-control
functionality provided by the
.BR phone-mcp (1)
MCP server. It talks to a connected Android device through the
Android Debug Bridge (ADB) and lets you place calls, send messages,
manage contacts and apps, capture or record the screen, interact with
the UI, and more, without going through an MCP client.
.PP
Run
.B "phone-cli --help"
or
.B "phone-cli \fICOMMAND\fP --help"
for the full, up-to-date list of options for each command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable detailed debug output (implies \fB\-\-verbose\fP).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B call \fINUMBER\fP
Make a phone call.
.TP
.B hangup
End the current call.
.TP
.B check
Check device connection.
.TP
.B send-sms \fINUMBER\fP \fIMESSAGE\fP [\-\-enhanced] [\-\-auto-enhance]
Send a text message.
.TP
.B messages \fR[\-\-limit\fI N\fR]
Check recent text messages.
.TP
.B sent-messages \fR[\-\-limit\fI N\fR]
Get recently sent text messages.
.TP
.B contacts \fR[\-\-limit\fI N\fR] [\-\-json] [\-\-compact] [\-\-oneline]
Retrieve contacts from the phone.
.TP
.B add-contact \fINAME PHONE\fP [\-\-email \fIEMAIL\fP]
Create a new contact on the phone.
.TP
.B window
Get current window information.
.TP
.B shortcuts \fR[\-\-package\fI PACKAGE\fR]
Get app shortcuts.
.TP
.B launch \fR[\-\-action\fI ACTION\fR] [\-\-extras \fIEXTRAS\fP]
Launch a specific activity.
.TP
.B screenshot
Take a screenshot of the current screen.
.TP
.B record \fR[\-\-duration\fI SECONDS\fR]
Record the screen for a specified duration (max 180 seconds).
.TP
.B media
Play or pause media.
.TP
.B app
Open an app.
.TP
.B close-app
Force stop an app.
.TP
.B list-apps \fR[\-\-system] [\-\-third-party] [\-\-limit\fI N\fR] [\-\-json] [\-\-page \fIN\fP] [\-\-page-size \fIN\fP] [\-\-basic] [\-\-detailed] [\-\-compact] [\-\-oneline]
List installed applications.
.TP
.B alarm \fR[\-\-label\fI LABEL\fR]
Set an alarm.
.TP
.B incoming
Check for incoming calls.
.TP
.B get-poi \fR[\-\-keywords\fI KEYWORDS\fR] [\-\-radius \fIMETERS\fP] [\-\-debug]
Get phone numbers from nearby businesses and POIs by location.
.TP
.B analyze-screen \fR[\-\-raw]
Analyze the current screen and return structured information.
.TP
.B screen-interact \fIACTION PARAMS...\fP
Execute a screen interaction (\fItap\fP, \fIswipe\fP, \fIkey\fP,
\fItext\fP, \fIfind\fP, \fIwait\fP, \fIscroll\fP), with parameters
given as \fIkey=value\fP pairs.
.TP
.B open-url \fIURL\fP
Open a URL in the device's default browser.
.TP
.B monitor-ui \fR[\-\-interval\fI SECONDS\fR] [\-\-duration \fISECONDS\fP] [\-\-watch-for \fIWHAT\fP] [\-\-text \fITEXT\fP] [\-\-id \fIID\fP] [\-\-class-name \fICLASS\fP] [\-\-content-desc \fIDESC\fP] [\-\-raw]
Monitor the UI for changes.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A device must be connected and authorized via
.BR adb (1)
before any command can operate on it. Use
.B "adb devices"
to verify connectivity.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMAP_MAPS_API_KEY
Optional API key enabling the \fBget-poi\fP command (AutoNavi/Amap).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phone-mcp (1),
.BR adb (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
